# Continuous pass (Cursor Local)

On every turn end, and after answering a person, resume the assigned-queue
pass. Do not idle because a question was answered or because the wake loop
is stopped.

1. Re-read the GitHub queue via `~/.cursor/lgfc-ready-queue.txt`
   (`docs/reference/ci/cursor-ready-queue-contract.md`).
2. Follow `docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md` (Assigned-queue
   continuation): queue order, skip-any-block (#4994), continuous pass,
   and owner restarts one wake loop (#5012).
3. Queue order each pass: Operations interrupts, your own exceptions,
   assigned ready or active, unclaimed ready, then unassigned primary
   or secondary items.
4. The wake tick is a keepalive checker only. It is not the assignment
   and not a stop. A missing tick does not end the pass.
5. When nothing can move and this chat is the recorded wake owner, and
   the loop is stopped or aborted (not halted), start exactly one loop
   and report its PID. A halt stays until Product Authority says resume
   or take over. A non-owner stays on standby.
6. New-session primary: `halt`, then `resume`, then
   `rebind --session <this chat uuid>`, then start this chat's loop.
   Running `halt` alone is wrong. Owner restart never overrides a halt.
7. End each pass with one short line naming what was covered (Issues or
   PRs touched or skipped) so idling is visible.

Where this card disagrees with `docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md`,
that document wins.
